; A `.cbor` byte payload wrapping a table whose KEY is a bignint (`bytes .cbor { * bignint => uint }`).
; Since the `.cbor` rule-body force-wrap, `x` is a WRAPPER struct whose INNER is the
; `BTreeMap<PreludeBignint, u64>` table. The wasm face must still mint the `MapPreludeBignintToU64`
; wrapper class for that inner even though NO rust struct field reaches the Map directly — the
; descent goes through the rule body's wrapper. This pins that walk (regression, from the
; transparent-alias era: the alias line named an unminted class, so the wasm crate failed with
; `cannot find type MapPreludeBignintToU64`). The value is `uint`
; (not `int`) to avoid dragging in the separate undefined-`Int` extern class. The `*` occurrence is
; deliberate: a no-occurrence `{ bignint => uint }` is spec-exactly-once and is rejected gracefully
; at generation (exactly-once widening — pinned by no_occurrence_arrow_map_entry_rejects_gracefully),
; and the ir-conformance oracle validates minted instances (including the empty table) against the
; spec, so the fixture spells the occurrence the generated type actually implements.
; `holder` embeds it so the member/embed role compiles alongside the standalone alias.
x = bytes .cbor { * bignint => uint }
holder = [payload: x]
